        <briefdescription>
<para>Calculate canopy eddy diffusivity. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Computes Eddy Diffusivity, Kz, within and just above canopy using stability-dependent parameterizations for different atmospheric conditions</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">HCM</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Height of canopy top (m) </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">ZK</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Above/Below canopy height, z (m) </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">USTAR</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Model input friction velocity (m/s) </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">MOL</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Model input Monin-Obukhov Length (m) </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="out">KZ</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Estimated Eddy Diffusivity with canopy turbulence (m²/s) </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="author"><para>P. C. Campbell </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>Jun 2022 </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Based on Makar et al. (2017) algorithms for canopy turbulence Makar, P., Staebler, R., Akingunola, A. et al. (2017). The effects of forest canopy shading and turbulence on boundary layer ozone. Nature Communications, 8, 15243. <ulink url="https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms15243">https://doi.org/10.1038/ncomms15243</ulink> Raupach, M. R. (1989). A Practical Lagrangian method for relating scalar concentrations to source distributions in vegetation canopies. Quarterly Journal of the Royal Meteorological Society, 115, 609-632. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
